            <ArticleTitle>Arylsulfonamide pyrimidines as VLA-4 antagonists.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3070-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2013.03.010</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(13)00326-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of (S)-2-(2-(diethylamino)-5-(N-alkyl-N-sulfonamido)pyrimidin-4-ylamino)-3-(4-(carbamoyloxy)phenyl)propanoic acid is discovered as orally available VLA-4 antagonists. Representative compounds 11b and 11p showed efficacy in multiple in vivo animal models. The in vitro selectivity of 11p is also described.</AbstractText>
